 ],
 "storyArc": "Tomás, Vale and Mariana travel to the Caribbean coast. Santa Marta is hot, slow and blindingly blue. In Taganga they meet Yesid Herrera, twenty-six, a diving instructor and the grandson of Joaquín, who died in 2010. If Joaquín were alive, Yesid says, he would be ashamed of the fight; if Yesid had money, he would buy his own boat. On the beach at night Tomás and Vale almost kiss, and then Mariana arrives with three beers."
